<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_6_2" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_6_2" name="6.2 Perform meter field work" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>6.2.1, 6.2.2 and 6.2.3 are drawn; 6.2.4 is a case with its own file.

EVERY PATH STARTS BY VERIFYING THE SERVICE POINT, and that is not ceremony. A meter operation performed at the wrong service point produces a correct field record against the wrong customer, and the error surfaces on a bill weeks later - by which time the crew, the meter and the evidence have all moved.

The final read on a removal and the initial read on a set are billing determinants, not asset attributes. They leave this group for 10.5 and 6.5, which is why 6.2.1 records them explicitly rather than treating the exchange as a swap.

6.2.2 IS A METER OPERATION, NOT A COLLECTIONS ACT. 10.4.2 and 10.4.5 disconnect and reconnect for non-payment and carry the customer protections that go with that; 6.2.2 operates the device on an authorised order from either source. Same physical act, different authority, and the safety check before operating is common to both.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_6_2_lanes">
      <lane id="l_62_field" name="Meter field technician">
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_sp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_kind</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_fin</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_op</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_new</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_safe</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_state</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_dev</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_link</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_pass</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_ok</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_case</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_close</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_62_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_62_start" name="An authorised meter order is received"><messageEventDefinition id="n_62_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_62_sp" name="Verify the service point and the authorised work"><documentation>6.2.1, 6.2.2 and 6.2.3. The commonest metering error is correct work at the wrong service point, and it surfaces on a bill, not on site.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_62_kind" name="Order type"/>
    <userTask id="n_62_fin" name="Record existing identity and final read"><documentation>6.2.1. A billing determinant - 10.5 closes the account on it.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_62_op" name="Set, exchange or remove the meter"><documentation>6.2.1.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_62_new" name="Record installed identity, seals and initial read"><documentation>6.2.1. Seals recorded at installation are what make a later tamper finding provable at 6.6.2.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_62_safe" name="Check field condition and safety controls"><documentation>6.2.2. Common to a planned turn-off and an immediate safety turn-off; only the authority differs.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_62_state" name="Operate the service device and confirm the state"><documentation>6.2.2.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_62_dev" name="Install the module or endpoint"><documentation>6.2.3.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_62_link" name="Record device identity and linkage"><documentation>6.2.3. The linkage is what 6.3.3 commissions against.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_62_pass" name="Pass the installed endpoint to commissioning"><documentation>6.2.3, into 6.3.</documentation></sendTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_62_ok" name="Completed as ordered"/>
    <callActivity id="n_62_case" name="Investigate condition or access (6.2.4)"><documentation>6.2.4. No access, a condition defect, or an identity that does not match the record.</documentation></callActivity>
    <serviceTask id="n_62_close" name="Close the field work record"><documentation>6.2.1.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <endEvent id="n_62_end" name="Meter work complete"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_start_n_62_sp" sourceRef="n_62_start" targetRef="n_62_sp" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_sp_n_62_kind" sourceRef="n_62_sp" targetRef="n_62_kind" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_kind_n_62_fin" sourceRef="n_62_kind" targetRef="n_62_fin" name="set, exchange or remove"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[order = "exchange"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_kind_n_62_safe" sourceRef="n_62_kind" targetRef="n_62_safe" name="turn-on, turn-off or reconnection"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[order = "state"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_kind_n_62_dev" sourceRef="n_62_kind" targetRef="n_62_dev" name="endpoint or module"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[order = "endpoint"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_fin_n_62_op" sourceRef="n_62_fin" targetRef="n_62_op" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_op_n_62_new" sourceRef="n_62_op" targetRef="n_62_new" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_new_n_62_ok" sourceRef="n_62_new" targetRef="n_62_ok" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_safe_n_62_state" sourceRef="n_62_safe" targetRef="n_62_state" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_state_n_62_ok" sourceRef="n_62_state" targetRef="n_62_ok" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_dev_n_62_link" sourceRef="n_62_dev" targetRef="n_62_link" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_link_n_62_pass" sourceRef="n_62_link" targetRef="n_62_pass" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_pass_n_62_ok" sourceRef="n_62_pass" targetRef="n_62_ok" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_ok_n_62_case" sourceRef="n_62_ok" targetRef="n_62_case" name="no access, defect or mismatch"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[completed = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_case_n_62_close" sourceRef="n_62_case" targetRef="n_62_close" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_ok_n_62_close" sourceRef="n_62_ok" targetRef="n_62_close" name="completed"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_62_close_n_62_end" sourceRef="n_62_close" targetRef="n_62_end" name=""/>
  </process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="dg_P_6_2">
